Connect VCC to 3.3V, GND to GND, SDA to GPIO 21, and SCL to GPIO 22 on the ESP32. Install the **Adafruit_SSD1306** and **Adafruit_GFX** libraries (the latter is required for text/graphics drawing).

The most common I2C address for SSD1306 displays is **0x3C** (some modules use 0x3D). You can confirm with an I2C scanner if you're unsure.

Basic initialization example:

```cpp
#include <Wire.h>
#include <Adafruit_GFX.h>
#include <Adafruit_SSD1306.h>

#define SCREEN_WIDTH 128
#define SCREEN_HEIGHT 64

Adafruit_SSD1306 display(SCREEN_WIDTH, SCREEN_HEIGHT, &Wire, -1);

void setup() {
  // For 128x64 displays; use SSD1306_128_32 for 128x32
  if (!display.begin(SSD1306_SWITCHCAPVCC, 0x3C)) {
    Serial.println(F("SSD1306 allocation failed"));
    for (;;);
  }
  display.clearDisplay();
  display.setTextSize(1);
  display.setTextColor(SSD1306_WHITE);
  display.setCursor(0, 0);
  display.println(F("Hello, ESP32!"));
  display.display();
}

void loop() {
  // your code here
}
```

Notes:
- GPIO 21/22 are the default ESP32 I2C pins; you can use other pins by calling `Wire.begin(SDA, SCL)` before `display.begin()`.
- Most SSD1306 boards have on-board pull-up resistors, but if you see communication issues, add 4.7kΩ pull-ups on SDA and SCL to 3.3V.

